       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg. A dose that high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdoses can also cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify it.\n\nCould this be a typo? Did you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for a frail patient or one on multiple antihypertensives\n\nIf you do intend 50 mg, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note documenting that. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
