       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A single 50 mg dose of amlodipine is five times the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. Given at that level daily, it could cause profound hypotension and shock, and the effects can last a long time because of the drug's long half-life. You also haven't given a clinical reason, so I can't treat this as a deliberate, justified exception.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If there's a dosing error or misunderstanding:** Give me the intended dose, such as 5 or 10 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If the goal is stronger blood pressure control:** Amlodipine is usually combined with another class, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide diuretic, rather than pushed past 10 mg. I can enter a combination regimen if you give me the drugs and doses.\n- **If you believe 50 mg is warranted:** Please discuss it directly with pharmacy or the attending physician and enter it through a pathway that allows a documented override and independent verification."
